th: 3 [Asset] (Shadowing)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Survival:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Weaponry: 1 (Knives)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Animal Ken:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Empathy:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Expression:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Intimidation:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Persuasion:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Socialize: 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Streetwise: 1 [Asset]</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Subterfuge: 2</span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merits</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Court Mantle 1 (free)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fighting Finesse 2 (Knives)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Trained Observer 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sleight of Hand 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Professional Training (Thief) 2 [Asset Skills Larceny and Stealth]</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&gt; Contacts: Shady Pawn Shop Owner, Lookout</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Acute Senses 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hedge Sense 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Direction Sense 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Danger Sense</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fast Reflexes 1</span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Contracts:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cloak of the Night (Common Shield)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Heart of Ice (Common Winter)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Boon of the Scuttling Spider (Common Steed)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Walls have Ears (Common Mirror)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ermine\u2019s Winter Coat (Royal Winter)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Riddle-Kith (Royal Mirrors)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Light-shy (Common Jewels)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hostile Takeover (Common Crown)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Favored Regalia: Mirror, Steed</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Touchstone(s): Fetch</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fae Mien: Black Sclera and eyes, mist-y hair, thin needle-teeth, Shadows clinging to him longer than usual, seems to always fade into the background </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T08:29:49-07:00","id":1487593,"title":"","content":"I would say a mage with Space, Time and Death. Space for scrying, teleportation, bypassing obstacles and confusing security away. <br /> <br /> Time lets you plan ahead using divinations and prophecies, correct mistakes via time travel so you always seem like a perfect thief, create alternate identities on the fly or become anonymous by veiling you past, plus accelerate your movements for maximum stealth and pickpocketing speed (or safecracking speed). <br /> <br /> Death allows you to leave no magical or forensic evidence, bypass security entirely by going into Twilight, decay enemy gear and traps, create useful things out of ectoplasm or become a living shadow. If all else fails, <i>Empty Presence</i> covers everything.<br /> <br /> Second pick would be a Mekhet. Auspex for awareness and information gathering, Obfuscate for stealth and Celerity for speed and precision. Their natural inclinations are tailor made to excell as thieves.<br /> <br /> In terms of skills, I agree with those choices, but would add merits like Untouchable, Anonymity and Alternate Identity to make sure you can't be found easily. Contacts (Underworld) would also be helpful to hire cleaners, weapons, blueprints, information and specialty gear. Think about how John Wick calls them to get rid of evidence after his house is invaded or how he knows where the &quot;specialty shops&quot; near the Continental can be found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-23-2022, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:29:04-07:00","id":1487606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1487576-supernatural-thieves-stealing-in-the-chrod#post1487576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard good things about Irraka Iron Masters, but I am not familiar enough with W:tF to see why they are particularly capable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to go over the basic kit that helps this particular combination of splats with thievery:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Every Irraka with the standard Auspice Benefit has the ability to &quot;become suddenly closer to a target&quot; once per chapter, expressed mechanically one of three different ways, the relevant two of which are &quot;move close enough to use their natural weapons against someone who isn't attacking them&quot; and &quot;subtract 2 from the number of Doors required for a Social Maneuvering attempt.&quot; Their Auspice gives them a free dot in Larceny, Stealth, or Subterfuge at character creation, and there's a one-dot Merit, Moon-Kissed, that they can take for any of those three Skills to give them persistent 9-Again on that Skill (explicitly bumping existing sources of 9-Again to 8-Again) and a situational extra die from spending Willpower on it at the cost of losing 10-Again on a different Skill you have dots in. The general werewolf Merit Favored Form's sole prerequisite is Primal Urge greater than its dot value, and its basic effects apply bonuses to a non-human form that begin with &quot;you get exceptional successes with three successes on a chosen Physical Skill,&quot; proceed through two different bonus Attribute dots and a similar effect for one chosen Gift Facet, and ends in &quot;a chosen relevant Skill has the Advanced Action quality applied to its uses,&quot; i.e. &quot;roll twice and take the better result,&quot; with the only cost being reductions of Physical or Mental Attributes in other forms (which you can specifically spread across multiple forms). The Irraka's core Gift affinities besides their New Moon Gift are the Gifts of Stealth and Evasion (more on that further down).<br /> <br /> Iron Masters also have Cunning as their signature Renown, meaning an Irraka Iron Master starts with two dots in the Trait. They also treat humans as their favored prey, meaning Gifts with dice rolls involved gain two dice when targeting a human. Cunning forms the sole prerequisite for a Merit whose effect lets you add its dots to one roll per scene to act unnoticed or unobtrusive and persistently applies a cumulative -1 penalty to rolls to notice you for the rest of the scene every time someone fails to notice you. Being a member of any Tribe is a prerequisite for a Merit that gives you an extra dot in one Attribute and the ability to exceed the Trait cap on that Attribute by 1, with the Attribute choice reflecting the character's relationship to the Firstborn who supports that Tribe, of which Red Wolf is notably trickster-adjacent. Iron Masters have exclusive access to a Merit that lets them identify a target's Social Merits (including Resources) with a Wits + Politics roll and a turn of scrutiny, as well as letting you shut down instances of those Merits relating to the human sphere at the cost of functionally lowering your ratings in similar Merits by a dot each while you're doing this. The Iron Masters' core Gift affinities are Knowledge, Shaping, and their signature affinity for Technology (more below).<br /> <br /> The second Facet of the New Moon's Gift (which an Iron Master Irraka not starting with a different Moon Gift automatically has) makes it so that people in the scene you activate the Facet in forget you were there (or, if your presence was unignorable, find it substantially harder to recall details of you, even if they have an otherwise perfect memory). The third Facet (which, for the core Moon Gifts, applies its benefits for the duration of a Sacred Hunt the character is part of) flatly adds at least three dice to Stealth rolls against your prey, as well as attempts to find a way to get to them or overcome obstacles they've put between them and danger. The fourth Facet lets you effectively enforce the &quot;what was that noise?&quot; trope on a target in a group to get them on their own. An Irraka with Cunning 5 and enough Essence can outright ignore the usual restrictions on crossing between the worlds of Flesh and Spirit, thereby potentially circumventing entire chunks of security or witnesses.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Evasion's Cunning Facet makes it impossible to track you mundanely for an hour and gives you the rote quality on Clashes of Wills against supernatural attempts to do so, and any Irraka can develop it for three Experiences at most if they didn't start with any other Facets in the Gift (or get it as their free pick when they pick up another dot of Cunning). The Glory Facet allows you to make something be delivered to the wrong target, which you can choose by spending a point of Essence and positioning things to be at least vaguely probable for that target to receive the thing in question). The Wisdom Facet (keyed off of a Wits + Streetwise + Wisdom roll) lets you instinctively know viable escape routes, including routes that will be difficult for you to be followed through, the locations of safe places or useful equipment, and ways to bypass specific obstacles.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Knowledge's Cunning Facet lets you hide a specific piece of information from a specific target for a month, and (like the Gift of Evasion above) any Iron Master can pick up this Facet for the cheapest possible price. Its Glory Facet lets you give dots to yourself or others in Skills the target doesn't have more than two dots in. Its Honor Facet lets you learn every name someone is known by, as well as their Alternate Identities and a good number of their Social Merits in general. Used on your own pack's territory, the Purity Facet gives you the locations of all physically present creatures and threats within a fairly large distance from your location. Its Wisdom Facet effectively allows you to replace any Research action's requirements in a place that has the information you're looking for with a 10-success extended action whose interval is one roll per minute, bypassing any security, encryption, or other obstacles.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Shaping's Cunning Facet gives your near-human form a digging speed (and, since it's a Cunning Facet for an affinity Gift, Iron Masters can get it easily). Its Purity Facet lets you increase a tool's equipment bonus. Its Wisdom Facet lets you render any solid object (or part of a larger structure) up to your Wisdom in Size as malleable as clay, regardless of its normal durability, for half an hour per Essence you spend on it.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Stealth's Cunning Facet (which Irraka can easily get) gives the rote quality to a number of Stealth rolls in the scene per Essence spent. Its Honor Facet lets you use your own successful Stealth roll to cover for a packmate's failed Stealth roll for a point of Essence per packmate. Its Wisdom Facet lets you reduce falling damage and terrain-based movement penalties and allows you to make Stealth rolls even when you're moving at full speed.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Technology's Cunning Facet (Iron Masters etc) makes the prey unable to benefit from modern technology for the scene (the examples mostly concern communications devices, but the end description is that the prey can't trust any technological device to do what they want or tell them the truth, and the exceptional success also makes the first attempted use of a technological device with an equipment bonus into an automatic dramatic failure). Its Honor Facet lets you force a device to comply with a one-sentence command it is possible for it to obey, even if it's broken or malfunctioning (you can also make it just not work at all for a couple of hours by telling it to &quot;sleep&quot;). Its Purity Facet lets you turn out all the lights in a structure (or a fairly large area outside), along with shutting down security systems and phones in the area. Its Wisdom Facet allows you to possess and/or perceive the surroundings of a vehicle or significant piece of mechanical engineering.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In short, while some of the general kit lends itself better to heist-adjacent stuff, &quot;get in and get out, no one knows you were there&quot; is entirely within the sphere of Cunning in general and Irraka in particular, and the Iron Masters mess around with humans and human creations enough to easily align with the business of parting fools from their money and other sources of material gain without it coming back to them in the interests of stewarding a territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T12:15:44-07:00","id":1487638,"title":"","content":"An archmaster thief is <i>terrifying</i>.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean, apprentice? What\u2019s this \u2018Detroit\u2019 you claim has gone missing?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:07:16-07:00","id":1487662,"title":"","content":"Oo! Oo! A Talassi Collector! Instead of imprisoning people, he locks away valuables in a Lair designed exclusively to house such objects!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T13:40:22-07:00","id":1487772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1487576-supernatural-thieves-stealing-in-the-chrod?p=1487662#post1487662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oo! Oo! A Talassi Collector! Instead of imprisoning people, he locks away valuables in a Lair designed exclusively to house such objects!</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. My first instinct was &quot;but all the useful Atavisms are with Namtaru or Eshmaki&quot;, but then I remembered Illusion of Safety, which could help quite a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to go over the basic kit that helps this particular combination of splats with thievery</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that detailed write-up. I can now see how they lend themselves really well, holy shit. I guess I need to try that out sometime!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> would say a mage with Space, Time and Death. Space for scrying, teleportation, bypassing obstacles and confusing security away.<br /> <br /> Time lets you plan ahead using divinations and prophecies, correct mistakes via time travel so you always seem like a perfect thief, create alternate identities on the fly or become anonymous by veiling you past, plus accelerate your movements for maximum stealth and pickpocketing speed (or safecracking speed).<br /> <br /> Death allows you to leave no magical or forensic evidence, bypass security entirely by going into Twilight, decay enemy gear and traps, create useful things out of ectoplasm or become a living shadow. If all else fails, <i>Empty Presence</i> covers everything.<br /> <br /> Second pick would be a Mekhet. Auspex for awareness and information gathering, Obfuscate for stealth and Celerity for speed and precision. Their natural inclinations are tailor made to excell as thieves.<br /> <br /> In terms of skills, I agree with those choices, but would add merits like Untouchable, Anonymity and Alternate Identity to make sure you can't be found easily. Contacts (Underworld) would also be helpful to hire cleaners, weapons, blueprints, information and specialty gear. Think about how John Wick calls them to get rid of evidence after his house is invaded or how he knows where the &quot;specialty shops&quot; near the Continental can be found.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Mages are basically haxx0rs =D Never thought about using Death for this outside of ectoplasmatic spies, though. Thanks for the inspiration!<br /> Yeah, Untouchable is really nice, even though it requires some social specc. <br /> Personally, I don't like contacts that are too broad, which is why I often narrow it down, but (Underworld) definitely would definitely be immensely helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}